Harsh-Review-Attacked: whether contention reads differently; std's File::try_lock and try_lock_shared take the same flock(2) lock fs2 took and report contention as TryLockError::WouldBlock, so every call site that read WouldBlock as another holder still does, and every other error keeps its io::Error.
Harsh-Review-Attacked: whether dropping the EACCES and EAGAIN contention test loses a holder; flock(2) with LOCK_NB reports a held lock as EWOULDBLOCK, which is EAGAIN on the platforms Stado runs on, and std maps that to WouldBlock; EACCES belonged to fcntl locks, which no caller takes.
Harsh-Review-Attacked: whether creating a run or an editor instance could now pass on a lock it does not hold; each try_lock that finds the new file held refuses naming it.
